    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay that makes sense. so if switching to thicker fabrics might dampen conductive contact, would it also help if i used something like a weighted lap pad or maybe a specific type of cushion between me and the chair? like something that could act as a buffer for the sensors to read my bio-signals more vaguely? i just want to make sure that if they're monitoring my focus levels, they aren't getting a clear picture of my actual stress levels.",
